[2.382864, "o", "\r\n=== iter 1 · run_benchmark({\"concurrency\": 1, \"enable_prefix_caching\": true, \"max_num_seqs\": 256})\r\nSince there are no previous metrics available, I am initiating a baseline probe to establish the current performance ceiling. I am starting with a high `max_num_seqs` and enabled prefix caching to determine if the system is currently memory-bound or limited by compute overhead at high concurrency.\r\n\r\n"]
[2.416816, "o", "/workspace/gemma-autopilot/autopilot/power.py:17: FutureWarning: The pynvml package is deprecated. Please install nvidia-ml-py instead. If you did not install pynvml directly, please report this to the maintainers of the package that installed pynvml for you.\r\n  import pynvml\r\n"]
[153.261574, "o", "\r\n=== iter 2 · run_benchmark({\"concurrency\": 32, \"enable_prefix_caching\": true, \"max_num_seqs\": 256})\r\nThe initial benchmark shows a very healthy TTFT (66.95 ms) well below the 500 ms limit, suggesting the current configuration is not latency-bound. However, with a concurrency of 1 and `max_num_seqs` at 256, we are significantly under-utilizing the H100's throughput capabilities. I will now aggressively increase concurrency to find the saturation point where throughput peaks before TTFT degrades.\r\n\r\n"]
[176.763477, "o", "\r\n=== iter 3 · run_benchmark({\"concurrency\": 128, \"enable_prefix_caching\": true, \"max_num_seqs\": 256})\r\nThe previous run at concurrency 32 achieved a high throughput of 1377.47 tokens/s with a TTFT of 255.02 ms, indicating significant headroom before hitting the 500 ms limit. By doubling the concurrency to 128, I aim to maximize the GPU's compute utilization and identify the point where queueing delays begin to push TTFT toward the constraint.\r\n\r\n"]
[178.938587, "o", "\r\n=== iter 4 · run_benchmark({\"concurrency\": 64, \"enable_prefix_caching\": true, \"max_num_seqs\": 256})\r\nThe request was rejected because it exceeded the hard guardrail of 64 concurrent requests. Since the previous run at 32 concurrency yielded a high throughput (1377.47 tokens/s) and a safe TTFT (255.02 ms), I will test the maximum allowed concurrency of 64 to find the upper bound of the throughput/latency trade-off.\r\n\r\n"]
[201.837479, "o", "\r\n=== iter 5 · run_benchmark({\"concurrency\": 64, \"enable_prefix_caching\": true, \"max_num_seqs\": 256})\r\nThe previous run at 32 concurrency showed high throughput with a TTFT of 255ms, leaving significant headroom before the 500ms limit. I am testing the maximum allowed concurrency of 64 to determine if the H100 can sustain higher throughput without violating the latency constraint.\r\n\r\n"]
[223.216065, "o", "\r\nLeaderboard:\r\n[\r\n {\r\n  \"label\": \"agent-iter-2\",\r\n  \"tokens_per_s\": 1377.47,\r\n  \"ttft_ms\": 255.02,\r\n  \"joules_per_token\": 0.3534,\r\n  \"score\": 1377.47,\r\n  \"rank\": 1\r\n },\r\n {\r\n  \"label\": \"agent-iter-4\",\r\n  \"tokens_per_s\": 1370.4,\r\n  \"ttft_ms\": 258.74,\r\n  \"joules_per_token\": 0.3498,\r\n  \"score\": 1370.4,\r\n  \"rank\": 2\r\n },\r\n {\r\n  \"label\": \"agent-iter-3\",\r\n  \"tokens_per_s\": 1357.47,\r\n  \"ttft_ms\": 261.57,\r\n  \"joules_per_token\": 0.3467,\r\n  \"score\": 1357.47,\r\n  \"rank\": 3\r\n },\r\n {\r\n  \"label\": \"human-expert\",\r\n  \"tokens_per_s\": 1289.42,\r\n  \"ttft_ms\": 297.33,\r\n  \"joules_per_token\": 0.3452,\r\n  \"score\": 1289.42,\r\n  \"rank\": 4\r\n },\r\n {\r\n  \"label\": \"vllm-defaults\",\r\n  \"tokens_per_s\": 405.68,\r\n  \"ttft_ms\": 121.16,\r\n  \"joules_per_token\": 0.768,\r\n  \"score\": 405.68,\r\n  \"rank\": 5\r\n },\r\n {\r\n  \"label\": \"agent-iter-1\",\r\n  \"tokens_per_s\": 57.89,\r\n  \"ttft_ms\": 66.95,\r\n  \"joules_per_token\": 4.3471,\r\n  \"score\": 57.89,\r\n  \"rank\": 6\r\n }\r\n]\r\n"]
